  // Swells roll toward the viewer as in the original: rows are born at the horizon and travel down, growing in height,
  // spacing and wavelength (perspective), each bobbing and drifting sideways. Every row look is painted ONCE, at the screen's
  // real pixel density, as a seamlessly repeating strip (3 looks x a ladder of depths). Per frame a row is filled with that
  // strip as a repeating pattern whose transform puts every crest exactly where the true wave is, so nothing jumps:
  // the shaded bands cross-fade between the two nearest depths, the crest lines and lace are shape-exact at any depth
